     kkvvmm__kkeerrnnddiisspp — get kernel displacement

LLIIBBRRAARRYY
     Kernel Data Access Library (libkvm, -lkvm)

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ##iinncclluuddee <<kkvvmm..hh>>

     _k_s_s_i_z_e___t
     kkvvmm__kkeerrnnddiisspp(_k_v_m___t _*_k_d);

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     kkvvmm__kkeerrnnddiisspp() returns the number of bytes by which the kernel referenced
     by _k_d is displaced.  This is the difference between the kernel's base
     virtual address at run time and the kernel base virtual address specified
     in the kernel image file.

     Note that if the kernel is moved to a lower memory address, the displace‐
     ment will be negative.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     kkvvmm__kkeerrnnddiisspp() returns the number of bytes by which the kernel is dis‐
     placed.  If the kernel is not displaced or if it is not possible to find
     the displacement then 0 is returned.

